 with scenes, character assets, score, and retry behavior. Match the project branch to your Godot version.","text","Access type","value","playable","demo","Play or run",[82],{"_49":83,"_25":84,"_73":85},"Play Squash the Creeps","https://godotengine.github.io/godot-demo-projects/3d/squash_the_creeps/","Official browser build with a moving character and enemy interactions. A WebGL-capable browser and keyboard are required.","Game platform","Browser","Build story / tutorial",[91],"tutorial",{"_49":92,"_25":93,"_73":-7},"Follow the official 3D tutorial","https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/getting_started/first_3d_game/index.html","list","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[99,100,101,102],"Play the browser demo and test movement, jumping, enemy contact, and retry.","Follow the official 3D game tutorial and compare its scenes with the completed project.","Ask an agent to adjust one mechanic, such as jump height or enemy spawning.","Replace one asset at a time and check collision shapes, scale, animation, and performance.","AI workflow / foundation context","Use the working project as an agent-readable reference for movement, collisions, animation, and score. Add generated assets only after the original game loop works.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","Human-authored engine foundation — not an AI-created game","category","provenance","Track","3D","track","metadata","Engine","Godot · 3D","engine","lead","3d",[99,100,101,102],{"_49":92,"_25":93},{"_49":83,"_25":84,"_17":78,"_73":85},{"_49":71,"_25":72,"_73":74},[125,126,127,128],"godot-engine","godot-demo-projects","godot-mcp","blender",{"_130":131},"documents",{"_132":133,"_134":135},"en",[137,141,142,143,140,144,145,146,147,148,149,150,151,152,153,154,155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,171,172,173,174,175,139,176,138,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197],"zh",[136,137,138,139,140],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill"